    {
        "id": "en:word:structure-on-the-other-hand",
        "label": "on the other hand",
        "fields": {
            "part_of_speech": "adverb",
            "pronunciation": ["/ɒn ði ˈʌðə hænd/"],
            "audio": "audio/7da2e8453f8bd4291a388594e5775acdbf2a210e22478d183d4e6d5ca7970e38.wav",
            "reference_images": [
                "images/796d0fbd00b357a84fa74c3a20cdfffe405efc79ef525e0048f6082a021d4eef.jpg"
            ],
            "usage_notes": {
                "en": "On the other hand introduces a contrasting consideration. Example: The city is exciting. On the other hand, the countryside is quiet. The two thought bubbles compare alternatives; the phrase is not about literal hands.",
                "de": "On the other hand leitet einen gegensätzlichen Gesichtspunkt ein. „The city is exciting. On the other hand, the countryside is quiet.“ = Die Stadt ist aufregend. Andererseits ist es auf dem Land ruhig. Die Gedankenblasen vergleichen Alternativen; Hände sind nicht wörtlich gemeint.",
                "id": "On the other hand memperkenalkan pertimbangan yang berbeda. “The city is exciting. On the other hand, the countryside is quiet.” = Kota itu menarik. Di sisi lain, pedesaan itu tenang. Dua gelembung pikiran membandingkan pilihan; frasa ini bukan tentang tangan secara harfiah.",
                "ja": "on the other handは別の対照的な観点を示します。「The city is exciting. On the other hand, the countryside is quiet.」＝都会は刺激的です。一方、田舎は静かです。二つの吹き出しは比較で、手を文字どおり指してはいません。"
            }
        },
        "class": "lexical:adverb",
        "tags": ["adverb", "sentence-structure", "grammar"],
